<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!DOCTYPE task PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA Task//EN" "task.dtd">
<task id="org-proxy-cache-configuration-api">
  <title>Configuring a proxy cache for an organization by using the Red Hat Quay API</title>
  <shortdesc>To create, validate, view, or delete a proxy cache configuration for an organization in Red Hat Quay, you can call the organization proxycache API endpoints with an OAuth access token.</shortdesc>
  <taskbody>
    <prereq>
      <ul>
        <li>You have created an OAuth access token.</li>
      </ul>
    </prereq>
    <steps>
      <step>
        <cmd>Use the <codeph>POST /api/v1/organization/{orgname}/proxycache</codeph> endpoint to create a proxy cache configuration for the organization.
</cmd>
        <info>
          <codeblock outputclass="language-terminal">$ curl -X POST "https://&lt;quay-server.example.com&gt;/api/v1/organization/&lt;orgname&gt;/proxycache" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer &lt;access_token&gt;" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
        "upstream_registry": "&lt;upstream_registry&gt;"
        "upstream_registry_username": "your_robot_account_username"
        "upstream_registry_password": "your_robot_account_password"
      }'</codeblock>
        </info>
      </step>
      <step>
        <cmd>Use the <codeph>POST /api/v1/organization/{orgname}/validateproxycache</codeph> endpoint to validate the proxy configuration:
</cmd>
        <info>
          <codeblock outputclass="language-terminal">$ curl -X POST "https://&lt;quay-server.example.com&gt;/api/v1/organization/{orgname}/validateproxycache" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer &lt;access_token&gt;" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
        "upstream_registry": "&lt;upstream_registry&gt;"
        "upstream_registry_username": "your_robot_account_username"
        "upstream_registry_password": "your_robot_account_password"
      }'</codeblock>
        </info>
      </step>
      <step>
        <cmd>Use the <codeph>GET /api/v1/organization/{orgname}/proxycache</codeph> endpoint to obtain information about the proxy cache. For example:
</cmd>
        <info>
          <codeblock outputclass="language-terminal">$ curl -X GET "https://&lt;quay-server.example.com&gt;/api/v1/organization/{orgname}/proxycache" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer &lt;access_token&gt;"</codeblock>
          <p outputclass="title">
            <b>Example output</b>
          </p>
          <codeblock outputclass="language-terminal">{"upstream_registry": "quay.io", "expiration_s": 86400, "insecure": false}</codeblock>
        </info>
      </step>
      <step>
        <cmd>Use the <codeph>DELETE /api/v1/organization/{orgname}/proxycache</codeph> endpoint to delete the proxy cache configuration:
</cmd>
        <info>
          <codeblock outputclass="language-terminal">$ curl -X DELETE "https://&lt;quay-server.example.com&gt;/api/v1/organization/{orgname}/proxycache" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer &lt;access_token&gt;"</codeblock>
          <p outputclass="title">
            <b>Example output</b>
          </p>
          <codeblock outputclass="language-terminal">"Deleted"</codeblock>
        </info>
      </step>
    </steps>
  </taskbody>
</task>
